UID:jan-van-eyck-residency-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261112T145239Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Jan van Eyck Academie Residency 2028 (Maastrich
 t\, 11 months)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Jan van Eyck Academie's
  general open call for its 2028 residency year: 30 to 32 artists\, curator
 s\, designers\, writers\, architects and other artistic researchers spend 
 11 months (15 January to 15 December 2028) in Maastricht\, across material
 -based and research-driven practices\, with access to the academy's labs a
 nd community.\n\nOrganisation: Jan van Eyck Academie\nLocation: Maastricht
 \, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settle in Maastricht an
 d register with the municipality (the academy applies for visas where rele
 vant).\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 1\,500 (EUR 2\,000 for participants 
 with children\; EUR 1\,500 per duo member or EUR 2\,500 combined for life 
 partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 combined\, max three stipends)\, w
 ith rent including service costs deducted from the stipend. Plus a EUR 2\,
 000 annual working budget and a newly built\, furnished private studio apa
 rtment. Application fee EUR 65 excl. VAT (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived fo
 r applicants from and living in OECD DAC-list countries\; enrolment fee fo
 r accepted participants EUR 2\,750 excl. VAT.\nDuration: 11 months\, 15 Ja
 nuary to 15 December 2028\; 30 to 32 positions\; selection outcome mid-May
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency
 -2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settl
 e in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the academy applies fo
 r visas where relevant).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mensch-maschine-visit-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261112T145239Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027
 : Energy Ghosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Mensch Maschine VISIT R
 esidency Program is an annual fellowship offering four fully funded fellow
 ships to artists from around the world\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the 
 Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with VISIT\, the artist-in-residence program
 me of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centr
 e for Contemporary Art (Warsaw).\n\nOrganisation: JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Ak
 ademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujaz
 dowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocation: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, 
 Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie der Künste\, Berlin (1 fel
 low)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to
  artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fellowships of EUR 20\,000 e
 ach\, intended for artist fees and production costs of a new project (rese
 arch and development\, travel\, materials and presentation costs)\, plus s
 tudio space and accommodation for the three-month residency.\nDuration: Ab
 out three months\, mid-August to mid-November 2027: retreat at Ujazdowski 
 Castle in Warsaw in mid-August\, then the residency at E-WERK Luckenwalde 
 or Akademie der Künste Berlin from late August\, ending with a symposium 
 at the Akademie der Künste on 5 and 6 November 2027. Fellows must be avai
 lable from 13 August to 10 November 2027 and live and work on site at leas
 t 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-m
 aschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
